to fallible memory.
<[Gary] GARY-S> at least you get to preview
<[Gary] GARY-S> I have yet to see a galley on any magazine I ever wrote for
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> What preview. I found one mistake, and I just now found 
another. (Sad look). I had stated that Bin a BEGIN...WHILE...REPEAT loop,
 the BEGIN..WHILE section was only exectued once.
<[Gary] GARY-S> short damn loop
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> I have not gotten galley proofs. Just looking back over 
the disk in preperation for the next column.
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> No. That the BEGIN...WHILE would execute once, and the 
WHILE...REPEAT would repeat while the flag was true.
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> When of course BEGIN...WHILE always executes once, and the 
whole thing executes so long as the flag is true.
<[Gary] GARY-S> writing your own constructs now ?
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> (Goes off to make phone call). I'll be back later on if I 
can.
<[Dave] DHWEINSTEIN> disconnected.
